<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borba (newspaper)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borba ('Struggle') was a Yugoslav communist newspaper founded in 1922 as an organ of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>. During the uprising of 1941 the Partisans printed it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a>, in the short-lived liberated territory known as the Republic of Užice. After the war it became one of the main official dailies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borba-newspaper.jpg" alt="Borba (newspaper)" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Borba editorial board · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borba_br_1_19021922_strana1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
